# v0.24.0 — Hub node development special

## V23-95 — Corrected ML circuits ported to the build tree

The `modular_ml_components` and `ml_training_verification` circuits were corrected in the coordinator-api tree under V23-94; this release ports the same fixed-point learning-rate checks to the `apps/zk-circuits` build tree and re-runs the ceremony so both trees hold byte-identical, contributed keys. `tests/unit/test_v2395_zk_circuit_tree_parity.py` now fails if the two trees diverge again.

## V23-96 — Pool Hub serves /health and describes outages instead of crashing

`pool-hub` now exposes a real `/health` endpoint. Before this change the `/health` path returned 404 and the monitoring infrastructure never watched the service. The monitoring and `health_check.sh endpoints` checks now treat `aitbc-pool-hub` as a first-class service.

## V23-97 — `is_not` operator fixed so billing sync can build a query

The Pool Hub SLA/billing query builder now emits the `is_not` operator correctly, allowing `/v1/sla/violations?resolved=true` to return 200 instead of 500. The CLI also aborts with a clear message when asked for per-pool SLA or when the host is unreachable.

## CLI — raw JSON, `balance_ait`, and `aitbc update`

- `aitbc account get` now shows `balance_ait` alongside the raw compute-seconds balance.
- `aitbc wallet balance` preserves the daemon's `balance`/`balance_ait` fields.
- `aitbc --output json` returns unwrapped machine-readable JSON.
- `aitbc update` pulls the latest `main` and runs `scripts/deployment/update.sh` in one command.

## V23-92 follow-up — shop/follower nodes stop treating hub-only services as local

`aitbc-exchange` (8106) and `aitbc-agent-coordinator` (8107) are hub-only. V23-92 already stopped coin-request notifications from defaulting to `localhost:8107`. The same default was still sitting in CLI config, pool-hub miner registration, and `health_check.sh`, so a shop node would report those units as down. Off-hub URLs now come from `HUB_DISCOVERY_URL` / `HUB_AGENT_URL` / `HUB_EXCHANGE_URL` in `/etc/aitbc/{blockchain,node}.env` (no baked-in hostname). `health_check.sh` now resolves the node role the same way `setup.sh` does and probes only that role's units and HTTP ports.

## Live verification

After the merges and restart on the hub node:
- `/health` returns 200 with `db`, `redis`, and `miners_online` status.
- `/v1/sla/violations?resolved=true` returns 200.
- `aitbc pool-hub status` and `aitbc pool-hub sla` return live data instead of simulated.
- `poolhub_miners_online` is exported on `/metrics` for Prometheus.
